# Desert Were-Worm: "for the first time each turn" means the first declaration this turn that reaches 12, so an earlier declaration of
# 11 does not use it up and one of exactly 12 does. Turn 9 (Bot1 has four Mountains and a Plains: the Worm is an 8/5): the Worm and
# Aurelia, the Warleader attack for 11 - no Worm trigger - and Aurelia's own trigger gives an additional combat. There they attack with
# a Memnite too, for 12, the first declaration to reach it, so the Worm triggers and gives one more combat. There the same 12 is not the
# first, so no fourth. Bot2 starts at 60: 11 + 12 + 12 = 35 damage, and the Worm, tapped by the last attack, was not untapped again.

